#import "release.typ": release, release-box, plain-words, signing
#show: release.with(
  title: "Kiki's Cat Club Foster Care Agreement",
  intro: [*Thank you for opening your home to a cat in need!* This is the agreement between you and Sun Brewed Homestead Inc. ("the Homestead") and its Kiki's Cat Club rescue program, for giving temporary care in your home to the cat or cats below. Please read all of it, especially the boxed release, and ask us about anything unclear before you sign. Below, "I" means you.],
  note: [Signed electronically. The signer must be 18 or older.],
  details: ("Cat(s) in foster care", "Foster start date"),
)

#plain-words[
- Foster cats stay ours. We pay for the vet care we approve, and we'll take a cat back whenever you need us to.
- Keep foster cats indoors and apart from your own pets until we say they can meet, and tell us about anything that worries you.
- *Fostering has risks, like scratches, bites and illness. You agree not to sue us over them, even if we were careless.*
]

*1. Ownership.* Every foster cat remains the Homestead's property. I will not sell, give away, rehome or adopt out a foster cat, or let anyone else take it, without the Homestead's written approval. If I want to adopt my foster cat, I will apply like any other adopter.

*2. Care.* I will provide food, fresh water, a clean litter box, safe indoor housing and daily attention. I will keep foster cats indoors, and apart from my own pets until the Homestead says they may meet. I will follow the care, feeding and medication instructions the Homestead gives me.

*3. Veterinary care.* The Homestead decides on and pays for veterinary care it has approved, at veterinarians it chooses. I will not seek non-emergency care without approval. In an emergency I will contact the Homestead immediately and, if I cannot reach anyone, take the cat to the nearest emergency veterinarian; the Homestead will then direct further care.

*4. Communication.* I will tell the Homestead promptly about any illness, injury, escape, bite or behavior change, and about any change to my address or ability to foster. I will bring foster cats to adoption events and appointments when asked, and the Homestead may share photos of them to find them homes.

*5. Ending foster care.* The Homestead may take a foster cat back at any time, and I will return it and any supplies the Homestead provided within 48 hours of being asked. If I can no longer foster, I will give the Homestead as much notice as I can, and never surrender the cat to a shelter.

#release-box(warning: [It gives up your right to sue us over fostering, including for our own carelessness.])[6. Release of liability and assumption of risk][
*I understand that caring for cats can involve scratches, bites, allergies, illnesses passed between animals and people, and damage to property, and that a foster cat may carry illness that could spread to my own animals. I assume these risks. To the fullest extent the law allows, I, for myself and my household, release, and agree not to sue, the Homestead and its directors, officers, volunteers, members and agents for any injury, illness, death or damage to people, animals or property arising from fostering, INCLUDING CLAIMS ARISING FROM THEIR ORDINARY NEGLIGENCE.* This does not release gross negligence, willful misconduct, the Homestead's duty to pay for veterinary care it approved, or any claim the law does not allow to be released.
]

#signing[*7. General.* I am a volunteer, not an employee or contractor, and I receive no payment for fostering. This agreement is governed by California law and continues for each foster cat I accept from the Homestead. If any part is held unenforceable, the rest remains in effect. I agree to sign electronically, and my electronic signature and initials bind me as if written by hand. *I am at least 18. I have read this agreement and had the chance to ask questions about it, I understand I am giving up substantial rights, including the right to sue, and I sign it voluntarily.*]
